3.4 Convergence of Iterative Proportional Fitting
In this section, we investigate the theoretical properties of IPF. When the state-space is discrete and finite (Franklin and Lorenz, 1989; Peyré and Cuturi, 2019) or in the case where pdata and pprior are compactly supported (Chen et al., 2016), IPF converges at a geometric rate w.r.t. the HilbertBirkhoff metric, see Lemmens and Nussbaum (2014) for a definition. Other than recent work by Léger (2020), only qualitative results exist in the general case where pdata or pprior is not compactly supported (Ruschendorf et al., 1995; Rüschendorf and Thomsen, 1993). We establish here quantitative convergence of IPF in this non-compact setting as well as novel monotonicity results. We require only the following mild assumption. A1. pN , pprior > 0, |H(pprior)| < +∞, ∫
