In this section, before recalling the usual definition of the IPF via potentials we provide a condition under which the IPF sequence is well-defined which is used throughout Section 3.2.
Proposition 25. Assume that there exists π ̃ ∈ PN+1 such that π ̃0 = pdata, π ̃N = pprior and KL(π ̃|π0) < +∞. Then the IPF sequence is well-defined.
Proof. We prove the existence of the IPF sequence by recursion. First, note that π1 is well-defined since π ̃ ∈ PN+1 with π ̃N = pprior and KL(π ̃|π0) < +∞. Second, assume that the sequence is well-defined up to n with n ∈ N. Using (Csiszár, 1975, Theorem 2.2) we have
